Subject: Align builtin's SUSFS callers with our pinned v2.2.0 GKI

Target: builtin 1cfa5734 after 12_align_builtin_1cfa5734_uapi6.patch.
CI 42534868339 failed because the newer builtin assumes priority UID, NO_SU
and zygote_next interfaces absent from the pinned SUSFS v2.2.0 source.

Keep the real b88403d2 CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS setresuid/umount implementation,
including its webview-zygote exclusion; leave the new mount-hide LSM intact.
Do not invent empty NO_SU/zygote_next helpers or advertise a priority command
that v2.2 does not implement. Priority calls exist only when its command does.
The UAPI6 dispatch, scoped su FD, preinit and paired SELinux parser stay intact.
Call the real GKI AV helper functions directly (no optional-pointer warnings).

